103†Page 3 … cite104†Page 19 --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRelease notes  |  Gemini API  |  Google AI for Developers (https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/changelog)\nciteturn806view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/changelog\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 949\nL0: [Button: ]\nL1: \nL2: [Input: Search]\nL3: \nL4: `/`\nL5: \nL6:   * English\nL7:   * Deutsch\nL8:   * Español – América Latina\nL9:   * Français\nL10:   * Indonesia\nL11:   * Italiano\nL12:   * Polski\nL13:   * Português – Brasil\nL14:   * Shqip\nL15:   * Tiếng Việt\nL16:   * Türkçe\nL17:   * Русский\nL18:   * עברית\nL19:   * العربيّة\nL20:   * فارسی\nL21:   * हिंदी\nL22:   * বাংলা\nL23:   * ภาษาไทย\nL24:   * 中文 – 简体\nL25:   * 中文 – 繁體\nL26:   * 日本語\nL27:   * 한국어\nL28: cite0†Get API key†aistudio.google.com cite1†Cookbook†github.com cite2†Community†discuss.ai.google.dev Sign in\nL29: \nL30: cite3†Docs cite4†API reference L31: \nL32: [Input: Filter]\nL33: \nL34: [Button: ]\nL35: \nL36:   * Get started\nL37: \nL38:   * Models\nL39:   * Robotics\nL40: \nL41:   * Core capabilities\nL42: \nL43:   * Image\nL44: \nL45:   * Video\nL46: \nL47:   * Speech and audio\nL48: \nL49:   * Thinking\nL50: \nL51:   * Agents\nL52: \nL53:   * Tools\nL54: \nL55:   * Live API\nL56: \nL57:   * Get started\nL58: \nL59:   * cite5†Thinking L60:   * Optimization\nL61: \nL62:   * Guides\nL63: \nL64:   * File input\nL65: \nL66:   * Logs and datasets\nL67: \nL68:   * Safety\nL69: \nL70:   * Frameworks\nL71: \nL72:   * Resources\nL73: \nL74:   * Migration\nL75: \nL76:   * cite6†Status†aistudio.google.com L77:   * Google AI Studio\nL78: \nL79:   * Google Cloud Platform\nL80: \nL81:   * Policies\nL82: \nL83: [Button: Send feedback ]\nL84: # Release notes\nL85: \nL86: This page documents updates to the Gemini API.\nL87: ## September 15, 2026\nL88: \nL89:   * Gemini 3.8 Live and Gemini 3.8 Live Extended Thinking generally available (GA): Released two new audio-to-audio models for real-time voice applications using the Live API:\nL90:     * Gemini 3.8 Live (cite7†`gemini-3.8-live` ): The default option for most low-latency voice agent experiences and real-time dialogue without reasoning delays. Features interleaved reasoning, default asynchronous function calling, and full session client content updates.\nL91:     * Gemini 3.8 Live Extended Thinking (cite8†`gemini-3.8-live-extended-thinking` ): High-reasoning audio-to-audio model supporting background reasoning during live audio interactions, recommended when higher background reasoning is required.\nL92: To get started, see the cite9†Live API guide , the cite10†Capabilities guide , and the cite5†Thinking guide .\nL93: ## September 3, 2026\nL94: \nL95:   * Lyria 3.5 generally available (GA): Released the next generation of Google's music generation model:\nL96: \nL97:     * cite11†`lyria-3.5` : Full-length song generation with improved musical coherence, natural vocals, and fine-grained duration and structural control.\nL98: \nL99: The model supports text and image inputs and generates high-fidelity 44.1 kHz stereo audio. See the cite12†Music generation guide for details and code samples.\nL100: ## September 2, 2026\nL101: \nL102:   * Gemini 3.8 Flash generally available (GA): Released `gemini-3.8-flash`, our most intelligent Flash model, engineered for long-horizon software engineering, autonomous agents, and complex enterprise workflows.\nL103: \nL104: To get started, see the cite13†Gemini 3.8 Flash model page and the cite14†Latest model guide .\nL105: ## September 1, 2026\nL106: \nL107:   * Agentic video understanding: Released agentic video understanding for Gemini 3.7 Flash, 3.6 Flash, and 3.5 Flash-Lite across the Interactions and GenerateContent APIs. The model dynamically navigates video timelines, requesting transcripts, frames, or audio tracks on demand. This approach uses up to 88% fewer tokens for long-form content compared to static processing.\nL108: \nL109: To get started, see the cite15†Agentic video understanding guide.\nL110: ## August 27, 2026\nL111: \nL112:   * Gemini Omni Flash generally available (GA): Released `gemini-omni-1.1-flash`, the GA version of our fast, conversational video generation and editing model. This release includes significant new capabilities:\nL113:     * Video extension: Seamlessly extend existing videos by generating continuations at the end of a clip using the `extend` task or directly with a prompt.\nL114:     * Interpolation (first + last frame): Generate a video transitioning between two images using the `image_to_video` task with up to 2 images.\nL115:     * Resolution control: New `resolution` parameter in `video_config` supports `360p`, `720p` (default), `1080p`, and `4k` outputs. 1080p and 4K outputs are generated using upscaling.\nL116: The existing `gemini-omni-flash-preview` endpoint will be deprecated on September 30, 2026.\nL117: \nL118: To get started, see the cite16†Gemini Omni Flash model page and the cite17†omni guide .\nL119: ## August 26, 2026\nL120: \nL121:   * Gemini 3.5 Transcribe generally available (GA): Released two dedicated speech-to-text models based on Gemini's audio understanding:\nL122:     * Gemini 3.5 Transcribe (`gemini-3.5-transcribe`): High-accuracy, low-latency non-streaming speech-to-text with utterance-based language detection across 85+ languages, speaker diarization, word-level timestamps, and custom vocabulary biasing (up to 1,000 terms).\nL123:     * Gemini 3.5 Transcribe Live (`gemini-3.5-transcribe-live`): Low-latency, bidirectional streaming speech-to-text over WebSockets using the Live API, supporting interim and finalized transcription events, Smart transcription mode, and multiple Voice Activity Detection (VAD) strategies.\nL124: To get started, see the cite18†Audio transcription guide , the cite19†Live transcription guide , and the cite20†Gemini 3.5 Transcribe model page .\nL125: ## August 13, 2026\nL126: \nL127:   * Gemini 3.7 Flash generally available (GA): Released our most intelligent workhorse model yet for coding and agents:\nL128: \nL129:     * Gemini 3.7 Flash (`gemini-3.7-flash`): Substantial improvements across software engineering, web development, and agentic workflows, available at an introductory price through December 31, 2026.\nL130: \nL131: To get started, see the cite21†Gemini 3.7 Flash model page and the cite14†Latest model guide .\nL132: ## July 30, 2026\nL133: \nL134:   * Gemini Robotics ER 2 in public preview: Released two new embodied reasoning model endpoints for robotics:\nL135: \nL136:     * `gemini-robotics-er-2-preview`: Advanced spatial reasoning, agentic code execution, multi-step tool orchestration, video moment finding, progress classification, and multi-robot coordination.\nL137:     * `gemini-robotics-er-2-streaming-preview`: Optimized for real-time text streaming using the Live API, enabling low-latency robot agents with bidirectional audio and video input.\nL138: Both model endpoints accept text, image, video, and audio inputs and support function calling with blocking behavior for physical robot actions. To get started, see the cite22†Gemini Robotics ER overview . For real-time streaming use cases, see cite23†Robotics with streaming .\nL139: \nL140:   * Deprecation announcement: The `gemini-robotics-er-1.6-preview` model will be cite24†shut down on August 31, 2026.\nL141: ## July 21, 2026\nL142: \nL143:   * Gemini 3.6 Flash and Gemini 3.5 Flash-Lite generally available (GA): Released stable, production-ready versions of our latest 3.x Flash models:\nL144:     * Gemini 3.6 Flash (`gemini-3.6-flash`): Features improved token efficiency and code/agentic planning capabilities at a lower price point than 3.5 Flash, resolving developer feedback around output verbosity.\nL145:     * Gemini 3.5 Flash-Lite (`gemini-3.5-flash-lite`): Offers a low-latency, highly cost-effective subagent option designed for high-volume automation.\nL146: \nL147: To learn more, see the cite14†Latest Gemini model guide.\nL148:   * Deprecated parameters: The sampling parameters `temperature`, `top_p` and `top_k` are now deprecated. See the cite25†Latest Gemini Model for details.\nL149: ## July 6, 2026\nL150: \nL151:   * cite26†Developer logs support for the Interactions API: logs for supported Interactions API calls are now viewable in the cite27†AI Studio dashboard†aistudio.google.com .\nL152: ## June 30, 2026\nL153: \nL154:   * Gemini Omni Flash in public preview: Released `gemini-omni-flash-preview`, a high-performance multimodal model designed for high-speed video generation and conversational video editing. Using the cite28†Interactions API , you can generate 3–10 second videos at 720p from text descriptions or animate still images, and then conversationally edit and refine the outputs. To get started, see the cite17†Gemini Omni Flash guide and the cite16†Gemini Omni Flash model card.\nL155:   * Released `gemini-3.1-flash-lite-image` (Nano Banana 2 Lite) to general availability (GA), our built-in multimodal model optimized for ultra-low latency and cost-effective image generation and editing. See the cite29†Gemini 3.1 Flash Lite Image model card and the cite30†Image generation guide.\nL156: ## June 24, 2026\nL157: \nL158:   * Computer Use: Launched public preview support for the cite31†Computer Use tool in Gemini 3.5 Flash. This release includes simplified actions with intents, built-in support for browser, mobile, and desktop environments, configurable safety policies, and advanced prompt injection detection.\nL159: ## June 17, 2026\nL160: \nL161:   * Streaming support for speech generation: Streaming via `streamGenerateContent` (and `stream: true` in the Interactions API) is now supported for the `gemini-3.1-flash-tts-preview` model. To learn more, see the cite32†Text-to-Speech guide.\nL162: ## June 15, 2026\nL163: \nL164:   * Deprecation announcement: The following image generation models are being deprecated and will be cite24†shut down on August 17, 2026:\nL165: \nL166:     * Imagen 4 and Gemini 3 Image models:\nL167:       * `imagen-4.0-generate-001`\nL168:       * `imagen-4.0-ultra-generate-001`\nL169:       * `imagen-4.0-fast-generate-001`\nL170: \nL171: To migrate your code to newer stable or preview endpoints, refer to the cite33†Gemini deprecations page.\nL172:   * Deprecation announcement: The following video generation models are being deprecated and will be cite24†shut down on June 30, 2026:\nL173: \nL174:     * Veo models:\nL175:       * `veo-2.0-generate-001`\nL176:       * `veo-3.0-generate-001`\nL177:       * `veo-3.0-fast-generate-001`\nL178: Update your integration to either use the Veo 3.1 preview model IDs (`veo-3.1-generate-preview`, `veo-3.1-fast-generate-preview`) or the 3.1 GA models available through the cite34†Gemini Enterprise Agent Platform†docs.cloud.google.com to avoid service interruptions.\nL179: \nL180:   * Deprecation announcement: The experimental GMP Contextual View tool (a fixed interface for Grounding with Google Maps outputs) will cite24†shut down on June 15, 2026:\nL181: ## June 1, 2026\nL182: \nL183:   * The following Gemini 2.0 models are now cite24†shut down :\nL184: \nL185:     * `gemini-2.0-flash`\nL186:     * `gemini-2.0-flash-001`\nL187:     * `gemini-2.0-flash-lite`\nL188:     * `gemini-2.0-flash-lite-001`\nL189: \nL190: Use cite35†`gemini-3.5-flash` or cite36†`gemini-3.1-flash-lite` instead.\nL191: ## May 28, 2026\nL192: \nL193:   * Released `gemini-3.1-flash-image` (Nano Banana 2) and `gemini-3-pro-image` (Nano Banana Pro), the generally available (GA) versions of our native visual models, cite37†Gemini 3.1 Flash Image and cite38†Gemini 3 Pro Image .\nL194:   * Video-to-image generation support: You can now pass a video file (via direct upload or as a public YouTube URL) as multimodal context alongside a text prompt to generate high-quality thumbnails, cinematic movie posters, or summary infographics. This feature is supported exclusively on the `gemini-3.1-flash-image` model. To learn more, see the cite39†Video-to-image generation guide.\nL195:   * Deprecation announcement: The `gemini-3.1-flash-image-preview` and `gemini-3-pro-image-preview` models are deprecated and will be cite24†shut down on June 25, 2026.\nL196: ## May 25, 2026\nL197: \nL198:   * The `gemini-3.1-flash-lite-preview` model has been cite24†shut down . Use cite36†`gemini-3.1-flash-lite` instead.\nL199: ## May 19, 2026\nL200: \nL201:   * Released `gemini-3.5-flash`, the generally available (GA) version of cite35†Gemini 3.5 Flash , our most intelligent model for sustained frontier performance on agentic and coding tasks. This is now the model behind `gemini-flash-latest`.\nL202:   * Launched the Managed Agents in the Gemini API in public preview. This enables developers to build and deploy autonomous, stateful agents that run in secure, isolated Google-hosted Linux sandbox environments. To learn more, see the cite40†Agents overview page and the cite41†Quickstart .\nL203:   * Released the general-purpose Antigravity Agent managed agent, cite42†`antigravity-preview-05-2026` , in public preview. The Antigravity agent can autonomously plan, reason, write and execute code, manage files, and browse the web inside its sandbox container. See the cite43†Antigravity Agent guide for code samples and specifications.\nL204: ## May 7, 2026\nL205: \nL206:   * Released `gemini-3.1-flash-lite`, the generally available (GA) version of cite36†Gemini 3.1 Flash-Lite , optimized for speed, scale, and cost efficiency.\nL207: \nL208:   * Deprecation announcement: The `gemini-3.1-flash-lite-preview` model is deprecating on 5/11/26 and will be cite24†shut down on May 25, 2026.\nL209: ## May 6, 2026\nL210: \nL211:   * Upcoming breaking change: The cite28†Interactions API request and response schema (`outputs` → `steps`) and output format configuration (`response_format`) are changing. The new schema becomes the default on May 26 and the legacy schema will be removed on June 8. See the cite44†migration guide for details.\nL212: ## May 5, 2026\nL213: \nL214:   * Updated File Search to support multimodal search. You can now natively embed and search through images using the `gemini-embedding-2` model. Grounding metadata now includes `media_id` for visual citations and `page_numbers` that indicate where information is found. To learn more, see the cite45†File Search guide.\nL215: \nL216: ## May 4, 2026\nL217: \nL218:   * Launched event-driven cite46†Webhooks support in the Gemini API to replace polling workflows for the Batch API and long-running operations.\nL219: ## April 30, 2026\nL220: \nL221:   * The `gemini-robotics-er-1.5-preview` model has been cite24†shut down . Use cite47†`gemini-robotics-er-1.6-preview` instead.\nL222: \nL223: ## April 22, 2026\nL224: \nL225:   * Released `gemini-embedding-2` as generally available (GA). To learn more, see the cite48†Embeddings page.\nL226: ## April 21, 2026\nL227: \nL228:   * Released new versions of the cite49†Deep Research agent with collaborative planning, visualization support, MCP server integration, and File Search:\nL229: \nL230:     * cite50†`deep-research-preview-04-2026` : Designed for speed and efficiency, ideal to be streamed back to a client UI.\nL231:     * cite51†`deep-research-max-preview-04-2026` : Maximum comprehensiveness for automated context gathering and synthesis.\nL232: ## April 15, 2026\nL233: \n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn806view2 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-16.json\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 1\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn806view3 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-16/transcript.md\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 1\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nReimagining advertising with AI | OpenAI (https://openai.com/index/reimagining-advertising-with-ai/)\nciteturn806view4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn804view0\",\"id\":14}); Total lines: 158\n"